      "rationale": "L1 and L2 both pin the junction to K423|G424 in mouse GDE2 (full-length, membrane-anchored), with L2 providing primer-level resolution. Python analysis of the human GDPD5 sequence confirms R423|G424 at the equivalent position (mouse K\u2192human R is a conservative substitution; G424 is identical). Position 423 lies deep within the large extracellular domain (topology span 214\u2013497), 209 residues from the proximal TM boundary and 75 residues from the distal TM boundary, satisfying the \u22653-residue clearance rule on both sides. Because the cited tag is in the mouse ortholog rather than the human protein itself, position_evidence is set to 'validated' (the residue is pinned to \u00b11 by primer sequence) and the site is classified as indirect. Transgenic mouse line expressing full-length mouse GDE2 with an external 3xFLAG tag inserted between K423 and G424 (mouse numbering), generated by Gibson cloning and confirmed by the Johns Hopkins Transgenic Mouse Core. Mouse GDE2 is the direct ortholog of human GDPD5; the junction residue differs conservatively (mouse K423 \u2192 human R423) while G424 is fully conserved. The forward Gibson primer (5\u2032-GGTCACATCCAGAAGCTG) encodes GHIQKL, matching human G424-H425-I426-Q427 exactly, confirming the junction maps to human position 423|424. The paper explicitly states the tag is placed 'externally (extracellularly)' in the intact membrane-anchored protein.",
