  "literature_notes": "L3 and L4 report surface biotin-labeling of 'GDE2-HA' in neuronal cell lines, confirming cell-surface display of the protein, but neither clip states where the HA tag is inserted; the naming convention 'GDE2-HA' and the truncation experiments in L5 suggest a C-terminal HA, which would be intracellular (residues 518\u2013605). Neither terminus of GDPD5 is extracellular, so topology_derived reasoning cannot rescue an unstated position. L3/L4 therefore do not qualify as surface-site evidence. L5 explicitly describes C-terminal HA and mCherry tags on full-length GDE2 used for truncation studies; the C-terminus (518\u2013605) is intracellular, so these are recorded in other_positions. L6 reports EGFP fused to the N-terminal end of full-length GDPD5 (EGFP-GDPD5) localizing to Weibel-Palade bodies and the plasma membrane in HUVEC; the N-terminus (residues 1\u201342) is intracellular, so this is an intracellular tag and goes to other_positions. L7 reports GDPD5-EGFP (C-terminal EGFP) with identical localization; again the C-terminus is intracellular. Only L1/L2 provide a pinned extracellular insertion site.",
